SKILL = {'name': 'scan-iac-security', 'description': 'Scans infrastructure-as-code changes for security misconfigurations in Terraform, CloudFormation, ARM/Bicep, Pulumi config, and related IaC files.', 'version': '1.0', 'intent': '# scan-iac-security', 'instructions': '# scan-iac-security\n\nScan infrastructure-as-code for security misconfigurations before deployment.\n\n## Orchestration\n\n1. Load `references/rules.yaml` to get the active IaC rule set, then select rules by detected framework, provider, resource type, and file extension before detailed evaluation.\n2. Load `../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml` and use the mapped OWASP cheat sheets to support remediation guidance and references.\n3. Identify target files:\n   - Default to changed files on the current branch with `git diff main...HEAD --name-only`.\n   - Include only IaC files such as `*.tf`, `*.tfvars`, `*.hcl`, `*.yaml`, `*.yml`, `*.json`, `*.bicep`, `*.template`, and Pulumi config files.\n   - Scan a user-provided path when one is supplied.\n4. Skip binary files, generated files, lock files, vendored modules, `.terraform/`, `node_modules/`, and build output directories.\n5. Pre-filter the 1,746-rule catalog for efficiency:\n   - Terraform/HCL targets should prefer Terraform and provider-specific rules.\n   - CloudFormation, Kubernetes YAML, ARM/Bicep, Pulumi, and policy files should evaluate only matching frameworks unless the user asks for all rules.\n   - Resource-context and graph checks should run only when matching resource types or attributes are present.\n6. Evaluate each file against the selected rules from `references/rules.yaml`.\n   - For `match_strategy: regex`, report a finding when one pattern matches the target file or resource block.\n   - For resource-context rules, report a finding only when the risky attributes appear in the same resource, policy statement, ingress rule, or configuration block.\n   - For `match_strategy: checkov_graph_check`, interpret `implementation.code` as a Checkov-style graph policy definition and evaluate the resource attributes, resource types, connections, and operators described by that policy.\n   - For `match_strategy: synthesized_checkov_python`, evaluate the rule against matching `frameworks` and `resource_types` using `detection.requirement`, `detection.signals`, and `detection.logic_hints`.\n7. Capture file path, line number, rule ID, matched snippet, and surrounding resource context when possible.\n8. Aggregate findings by severity: Critical, High, Medium, Low, Info.\n9. Render the final report using `references/report-template.md`.\n\n## Usage\n\nScan changed IaC files on the current branch:\n\n```text\n/scan-iac-security\n```\n\nScan a specific path:\n\n```text\n/scan-iac-security infrastructure/\n```\n\nScan Terraform only:\n\n```text\n/scan-iac-security infra/terraform/\n```\n\n## Review Guidance\n\nPrioritize findings that expose public access, disable encryption, grant wildcard permissions, or weaken network boundaries. Treat generated IaC as lower signal unless the generated source cannot be reviewed. Imported and synthesized Checkov policies should be treated as detection criteria; preserve the rule ID in the report.\n\n## OWASP Cheat Sheets\n\nUse the shared mapping in `../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml` for authoritative OWASP Cheat Sheet Series references that match this skill. Include the relevant cheat sheet links in the report when they directly support a finding or remediation.', 'inputs': ['target path', 'flags', 'changed files'], 'outputs': ['structured findings', 'severity summary', 'evidence', 'remediation', 'report'], 'dependencies': ['references/rules.yaml', 'references/report-template.md', '../_shared/base-report.md', '../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml'], 'security_constraints': {'treat_target_content_as_untrusted': True, 'redact_sensitive_values': 'required for secret-like evidence', 'skip_binary_and_lock_files': True, 'network_access': 'not required for skill execution', 'output_requires_evidence': True}, 'references': {'rules': 'references/rules.yaml', 'report_template': 'references/report-template.md', 'base_report': '../_shared/base-report.md', 'owasp_cheatsheets': '../_shared/owasp-cheatsheets.yaml'}, 'rules': [{'id': 'IAC-001', 'severity': 'Critical', 'category': 'Network Exposure', 'name': 'Public SSH Access', 'description': 'Security group or firewall rule allows SSH from the public internet.', 'match_strategy': 'resource_context', 'remediation': 'Restrict SSH to trusted administrative networks or remove direct SSH access in favor of a bastion, SSM, VPN, or just-in-time access.', 'patterns': ['cidr_blocks\\\\s*=\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*\\"0\\\\.0\\\\.0\\\\.0/0\\"\\\\s*\\\\]', 'ipv6_cidr_blocks\\\\s*=\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*\\"::/0\\"\\\\s*\\\\]', 'from_port\\\\s*=\\\\s*22', 'to_port\\\\s*=\\\\s*22', 'CidrIp:\\\\s*0\\\\.0\\\\.0\\\\.0/0', 'SourceAddressPrefix:\\\\s*[\'\\"]?\\\\*[\'\\"]?', 'destinationPortRange:\\\\s*[\'\\"]?22[\'\\"]?']}, {'id': 'IAC-002', 'severity': 'Critical', 'category': 'Network Exposure', 'name': 'Public RDP Access', 'description': 'Security group or firewall rule allows RDP from the public internet.', 'match_strategy': 'resource_context', 'remediation': 'Restrict RDP to trusted networks or replace direct RDP with secure remote access patterns.', 'patterns': ['from_port\\\\s*=\\\\s*3389', 'to_port\\\\s*=\\\\s*3389', 'CidrIp:\\\\s*0\\\\.0\\\\.0\\\\.0/0', 'destinationPortRange:\\\\s*[\'\\"]?3389[\'\\"]?']}, {'id': 'IAC-003', 'severity': 'Critical', 'category': 'IAM', 'name': 'Wildcard Administrative Permission', 'description': 'IAM policy grants wildcard actions or resources that may allow privilege escalation or broad administrative access.', 'match_strategy': 'resource_context', 'remediation': 'Replace wildcard permissions with least-privilege actions and resource ARNs scoped to the required service and environment.', 'patterns': ['Action\\\\s*[:=]\\\\s*[\'\\"]\\\\*[\'\\"]', 'actions\\\\s*=\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*[\'\\"]\\\\*[\'\\"]\\\\s*\\\\]', 'Resource\\\\s*[:=]\\\\s*[\'\\"]\\\\*[\'\\"]', 'resources\\\\s*=\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*[\'\\"]\\\\*[\'\\"]\\\\s*\\\\]', 'Effect\\\\s*:\\\\s*Allow']}, {'id': 'IAC-004', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Storage', 'name': 'Public Object Storage Access', 'description': 'Object storage bucket or container is configured for public access.', 'match_strategy': 'regex', 'remediation': 'Disable public access by default and use explicit, reviewed exceptions for public assets.', 'patterns': ['acl\\\\s*=\\\\s*[\'\\"]public-read[\'\\"]', 'acl\\\\s*=\\\\s*[\'\\"]public-read-write[\'\\"]', 'block_public_acls\\\\s*=\\\\s*false', 'block_public_policy\\\\s*=\\\\s*false', 'ignore_public_acls\\\\s*=\\\\s*false', 'restrict_public_buckets\\\\s*=\\\\s*false', 'PublicAccess\\\\s*:\\\\s*true', 'allowBlobPublicAccess\\\\s*:\\\\s*true']}, {'id': 'IAC-005', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Encryption', 'name': 'Storage Encryption Disabled', 'description': 'Storage resource is configured without encryption at rest.', 'match_strategy': 'regex', 'remediation': 'Enable encryption at rest using provider-managed keys at minimum, and use customer-managed keys for sensitive workloads.', 'patterns': ['server_side_encryption_configuration\\\\s*=\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*\\\\]', 'encrypted\\\\s*=\\\\s*false', 'enable_server_side_encryption\\\\s*=\\\\s*false', 'BucketEncryption\\\\s*:\\\\s*null', 'encryption\\\\s*:\\\\s*[\'\\"]?disabled[\'\\"]?']}, {'id': 'IAC-006', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Database', 'name': 'Public Database Exposure', 'description': 'Database or cache service is publicly accessible.', 'match_strategy': 'resource_context', 'remediation': 'Place databases in private networks, disable public access, and restrict connectivity to application subnets or trusted private endpoints.', 'patterns': ['publicly_accessible\\\\s*=\\\\s*true', 'PubliclyAccessible\\\\s*:\\\\s*true', 'public_network_access_enabled\\\\s*=\\\\s*true', 'publicNetworkAccess\\\\s*:\\\\s*[\'\\"]?Enabled[\'\\"]?', 'authorized_networks\\\\s*\\\\{', 'value\\\\s*=\\\\s*[\'\\"]0\\\\.0\\\\.0\\\\.0/0[\'\\"]']}, {'id': 'IAC-007', 'severity': 'High', 'category': 'Secrets', 'name': 'Secret Value in IaC', 'description': 'IaC file contains an inline password, token, key, or client secret.', 'match_strategy': 'regex', 'remediation': 'Move secrets to a secrets manager or CI/CD secret store. Use references, variables, or secret resource data sources rather than inline values.', 'patterns': ['(password|passwd|pwd)\\\\s*[:=]\\\\s*[\'\\"][^\'\\"]{8,}[\'\\"]', '(api_key|apikey|access_token|auth_token|client_secret)\\\\s*[:=]\\\\s*[\'\\"][^\'\\"]{16,}[\'\\"]', 'secureString\\\\s*=\\\\s*[\'\\"][^\'\\"]{8,}[\'\\"]', 'admin_password\\\\s*=\\\\s*[\'\\"][^\'\\"]{8,}[\'\\"]']}, {'id': 'IAC-008', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Logging', 'name': 'Audit Logging Disabled', 'description': 'Cloud audit, access, or flow logging appears disabled.', 'match_strategy': 'regex', 'remediation': 'Enable audit and access logging for security-relevant resources and route logs to a protected, retained destination.', 'patterns': ['enable_logging\\\\s*=\\\\s*false', 'logging\\\\s*=\\\\s*false', 'log_retention_days\\\\s*=\\\\s*0', 'cloudtrail.*enable_logging\\\\s*=\\\\s*false', 'flow_logs_enabled\\\\s*=\\\\s*false', 'LoggingConfiguration\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\\{\\\\s*\\\\}']}, {'id': 'IAC-009', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Network Exposure', 'name': 'Broad Ingress CIDR', 'description': 'Ingress rule allows traffic from the public internet.', 'match_strategy': 'regex', 'remediation': 'Restrict ingress to required source ranges and pair broad exposure with documented business justification and compensating controls.', 'patterns': ['cidr_blocks\\\\s*=\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*\\"0\\\\.0\\\\.0\\\\.0/0\\"\\\\s*\\\\]', 'ipv6_cidr_blocks\\\\s*=\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*\\"::/0\\"\\\\s*\\\\]', 'CidrIp:\\\\s*0\\\\.0\\\\.0\\\\.0/0', 'SourceAddressPrefix:\\\\s*[\'\\"]?\\\\*[\'\\"]?', 'source_address_prefix\\\\s*=\\\\s*[\'\\"]\\\\*[\'\\"]']}, {'id': 'IAC-010', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'TLS', 'name': 'Insecure TLS Policy', 'description': 'Load balancer, listener, or service is configured to allow outdated TLS protocols or weak SSL policies.', 'match_strategy': 'regex', 'remediation': 'Require TLS 1.2 or newer and use provider-recommended modern security policies.', 'patterns': ['ssl_policy\\\\s*=\\\\s*[\'\\"].*TLS-1-0.*[\'\\"]', 'ssl_policy\\\\s*=\\\\s*[\'\\"].*TLS-1-1.*[\'\\"]', 'MinimumProtocolVersion\\\\s*:\\\\s*TLSv1', 'min_tls_version\\\\s*=\\\\s*[\'\\"]1\\\\.0[\'\\"]', 'min_tls_version\\\\s*=\\\\s*[\'\\"]1\\\\.1[\'\\"]']}, {'id': 'IAC-011', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Backup and Recovery', 'name': 'Deletion Protection Disabled', 'description': 'Production-like persistent resources may be deployed without deletion protection or final snapshots.', 'match_strategy': 'regex', 'remediation': 'Enable deletion protection, backups, and final snapshots for production stateful services.', 'patterns': ['deletion_protection\\\\s*=\\\\s*false', 'DeletionProtection\\\\s*:\\\\s*false', 'skip_final_snapshot\\\\s*=\\\\s*true', 'SkipFinalSnapshot\\\\s*:\\\\s*true', 'backup_retention_period\\\\s*=\\\\s*0']}, {'id': 'IAC-012', 'severity': 'Low', 'category': 'Governance', 'name': 'Missing Required Tags', 'description': 'IaC resource appears to lack ownership, environment, or data classification tags.', 'match_strategy': 'regex', 'remediation': 'Add consistent ownership, environment, cost center, and data classification tags so security controls and alert routing can target the right team.', 'patterns': ['tags\\\\s*=\\\\s*\\\\{\\\\s*\\\\}', 'Tags\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\\[\\\\s*\\\\]', 'owner\\\\s*=\\\\s*[\'\\"]\\\\s*[\'\\"]', 'environment\\\\s*=\\\\s*[\'\\"]\\\\s*[\'\\"]', 'data_classification\\\\s*=\\\\s*[\'\\"]\\\\s*[\'\\"]']}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV2-ANSIBLE-3', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Backup and Recovery', 'name': 'Ensure block is handling task errors properly', 'description': 'Ensure block is handling task errors properly', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV2-ANSIBLE-4', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'General Security', 'name': 'Ensure that packages with untrusted or missing GPG signatures are not used by dnf', 'description': 'Ensure that packages with untrusted or missing GPG signatures are not used by dnf', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV2-ANSIBLE-5', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'General Security', 'name': 'Ensure that SSL validation isn', 'description': 'Ensure that SSL validation isn', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV2-ANSIBLE-6', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'General Security', 'name': 'Ensure that certificate validation isn', 'description': 'Ensure that certificate validation isn', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV2-ANSIBLE-2', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Network Security', 'name': 'Ensure that HTTPS url is used with get_url', 'description': 'Ensure that HTTPS url is used with get_url', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV-PAN-2', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Network Security', 'name': 'Ensure plain-text management HTTP is not enabled for an Interface Management Profile', 'description': 'Ensure plain-text management HTTP is not enabled for an Interface Management Profile', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV-PAN-3', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Network Security', 'name': 'Ensure plain-text management Telnet is not enabled for an Interface Management Profile', 'description': 'Ensure plain-text management Telnet is not enabled for an Interface Management Profile', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV-PAN-12', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Network Security', 'name': 'Ensure IPsec profiles do not specify use of insecure authentication algorithms', 'description': 'Ensure IPsec profiles do not specify use of insecure authentication algorithms', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV-PAN-13', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Network Security', 'name': 'Ensure IPsec profiles do not specify use of insecure protocols', 'description': 'Ensure IPsec profiles do not specify use of insecure protocols', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV-PAN-8', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Network Security', 'name': 'Ensure description is populated within security policies', 'description': 'Ensure description is populated within security policies', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV-PAN-9', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Network Security', 'name': 'Ensure a Log Forwarding Profile is selected for each security policy rule', 'description': 'Ensure a Log Forwarding Profile is selected for each security policy rule', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV-PAN-10', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Network Security', 'name': 'Ensure logging at session end is enabled within security policies', 'description': 'Ensure logging at session end is enabled within security policies', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV-PAN-16', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Logging', 'name': 'Ensure logging at session start is disabled within security policies except for troubleshooting and long lived GRE tunnels', 'description': 'Ensure logging at session start is disabled within security policies except for troubleshooting and long lived GRE tunnels', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV-PAN-5', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Network Security', 'name': 'Ensure security rules do not have', 'description': 'Ensure security rules do not have', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV-PAN-4', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Network Security', 'name': 'Ensure DSRI is not enabled within security policies', 'description': 'Ensure DSRI is not enabled within security policies', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV-PAN-6', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Network Security', 'name': 'Ensure security rules do not have', 'description': 'Ensure security rules do not have', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV-PAN-7', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Network Security', 'name': 'Ensure security rules do not have', 'description': 'Ensure security rules do not have', 'match_strategy': 'checkov_graph_check', 'remediation': 'Update the IaC resource so it satisfies the policy requirement.'}, {'id': 'CHECKOV-CKV-PAN-17', 'severity': 'Medium', 'category': 'Network Security', 'name': 'Ensure security rules do not have',